00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.950
Be sure to go check out and subscribe to Real
Engineering’s channel.

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:08.490
If you like this channel, I guarantee you
will enjoy his.

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:12.912
I’ll leave you with the real reason specific
airfares are expensive, but also a reason

00:09:12.912 --> 00:09:15.750
why they’re getting cheaper—competition,
or lack there of.

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:19.270
The airline industry is one with very little
competition.

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:23.100
Airfares from New York to LA are cheap because
there’s a lot of demand and there’s a

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.840
relatively high amount of competition.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:31.080
Five different airlines fly direct from New
York to LA, two of which are budget airlines.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:35.710
People don’t care that much which airline
they fly, they care about the price, so airlines

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:38.730
will try to match the price of the budget
airlines.

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:42.450
Compare this to a route like Denver to Gunnison
Country airport.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:47.390
Largely because only United makes this flight,
you will often pay more than $500 for this

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:48.980
130 mile flight.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:52.290
So, that’s why your plane tickets cost so
much.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:57.000
Next time you book your travel, you’ll know
why you’re paying so much and also how little

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.920
of that actually goes to airlines.

